openstack-nova — OpenStack Compute service (Nova) 34.0.0 (2026.2 Hibiscus)
=========================================================================

This package installs the Nova compute service: API, conductor,
scheduler, compute agent and the noVNC/serial/SPICE console proxies.
It installs software ONLY: nothing is enabled, started, migrated or
credentialed at install time.

What it ships
-------------

  /usr/bin/nova-*                 administrative CLIs and daemons
                                  (compute, conductor, manage, novncproxy,
                                  scheduler, serialproxy,
                                  spicehtml5proxy, status, ...)
  nova.wsgi.osapi_compute:application   the supported WSGI application
  nova/db/{api,main}/migrations/  database migration scripts
  /etc/nova/api-paste.ini         upstream paste pipeline (wiring)
  /etc/nova/rootwrap.conf + rootwrap.d/compute.filters
  /etc/init.d/nova-*              OpenRC services (7 daemons)
  /usr/lib/systemd/system/nova-*.service   systemd services (7 daemons)
  /etc/conf.d/nova-*              WSGI container runtime settings (api)

Operator steps (NOT performed by this package)
----------------------------------------------

1. Write /etc/nova/nova.conf (database, keystone auth, libvirt,
   VNC/serial/SPICE consoles, Neutron networking, placement, ...).
   Render the skeleton from the shipped generator inputs:

     oslo-config-generator \
       --config-file /usr/share/nova/nova-config-generator.conf \
       --output-file /etc/nova/nova.conf
   # edit /etc/nova/nova.conf. No database driver is installed by this
   # package: add python-pymysql for MariaDB, or use sqlite for trials.

2. Initialise the databases (api first, then cell0 and cell1):

     nova-manage api_db sync
     nova-manage cell_v2 map_cell0
     nova-manage cell_v2 create_cell --name=cell1 ...
     nova-manage db sync

3. Register the service and endpoints in Keystone (operator-chosen).

4. Enable per node role, explicitly. Controller example:

     rc-update add nova-api default && rc-service nova-api start
     rc-update add nova-conductor default && ...
     rc-update add nova-scheduler default && ...
   Compute node example:

     rc-update add nova-compute default && rc-service nova-compute start
   (systemd: systemctl enable --now nova-<daemon> instead.)

Nova-compute drives KVM through libvirtd: the libvirt daemons must be
installed and running, with QEMU/KVM available. The daemons talk to
libvirtd, never to qemu binaries directly.

Independence
------------

Nova depends on the native python closure, gunicorn, libvirt bindings
and database client libraries. It does not depend on Neutron, Cinder,
Glance placement beyond API calls, Horizon or QEMU directly, and it
can be installed on its own.
